      "message": "Let a landed commit be given a name, once\n\nA forge that refuses every tag cannot have a tagged release. Tags now\nreach the proc-receive hook like changes do: the hook peels the tag,\nrefuses a commit that is not on any branch, and asks the forge; the\nforge records a `tag_pushed` event when the pusher holds merge on the\nrepository and the name is new. A tag is never moved or deleted — a\nlater tag is a new statement, not a correction — and the pre-receive\nguard still closes every other write path. Annotated tags keep their\nmessage. The tags table is a projection (schema 25); repositories list\ntheirs at /api/repos/{name}/tags, follow renames and deletion, and the\nmirror carries tags with the branches, pushed the moment the ref exists\nrather than at the next landing. The hook scripts are reinstalled before\nevery receive, so repositories created by an older forge take tags too.\n\nChange-Id: Itags0090named\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
